; Psychonauts on the DS4 (milestone l, docs/ps4/HANDOFF-i.md): xinput mode. The title gives the DS4 to the game
; as XInput controller 0 (pw_wine_game_pad's mapping), and the game's own pad bindings do the rest. With the
; game's Defaults (Options, Bindings), read from Psychonauts.exe's XInput read at 0x406332 and its name table
; at 0x782820 + code*4:
;
;   square    Joy1  X      Attack            l2  Joy5  LT   LockOn/Float (any trigger value above 0)
;   cross     Joy2  A      Jump              r2  Joy6  RT   PsiPower1
;   circle    Joy3  B      Cancel            r1  Joy7  RB   PsiPower2
;   triangle  Joy4  Y      Use               l1  Joy8  LB   PsiPower3
;   options   Joy9  Start  Journal           l3  Joy11 LS   Stats
;   touchpad left half  Joy10 Back (unbound) r3  Joy12 RS   FirstPerson
;   touchpad right half       the title's mark, never given to the game
;   d-pad left/right          InventoryMenu / PsiPowersMenu; the sticks walk and turn the camera
;
; One key is posted beside the pad: Enter, on the touchpad's left half, for the first launch's new-profile
; screen (the bunk bed and the name), which takes Enter from the keyboard and nothing from the pad. Not on
; cross or options: the EXE also reads A (0x519261) and Start (0x519620) directly, so Enter on cross could
; confirm two screens with one press, and Escape on options could open and close the Journal at once. Back
; (0x121) is read nowhere but the XInput read and no default binds Joy10, so the left half does one thing.
; No Escape: circle cancels in the menus.
[input]
mode = xinput
touchpad_left = enter
